#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:5
#: 2f3818497ec141b9a07cd5c969b6ec69
msgid "Telemetry / Serial Port Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:7
#: 02b4ace0f83d42eea40c7d8f8a7b04d6
msgid "This article shows how to configure the telemetry ports (aka serial ports) on the autopilot. The instructions use the Pixhawk but they apply for most autopilots."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:11
#: b76acf13bf3440189688aef631bb1ce3
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:13
#: bc49160373894a4599eef159795f009b
msgid "On a Pixhawk there are a total of 5 serial ports.  The default use of each port is:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:15
#: 1fc30c9a62044900b482928f2fae4117
msgid "The micro USB port (aka Serial0) is used to connect to the ground station using a USB cable.  This should not be connected in flight because the flight code assumes that if it is receiving power through this port that it is on the bench and some :ref:`failsafes <copter:failsafe-landing-page>` (i.e. battery failsafe) are disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:16
#: f75188d86ce149e98170d4cf8b83d5b9
msgid "Telem1 (aka Serial1) is for MAVLink communication and supports flow control.  This should be used especially for high power devices (up to 1 amp) But NOT the :ref:`RFD900 telemetry radio <common-rfd900>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:18
#: 823e0f8b640b46e3a2d49289955cb7e3
msgid "Many non-Pixhawk style autopilots CANNOT supply even 1 amp on their port supply lines. Be sure to verify with autopilots specifications. If not specified, limit current to < 200 ma."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:20
#: dd8039b8a609422e90498754c1872ff7
msgid "Telem2 (aka Serial2) is for MAVLink communication and supports flow control."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:21
#: e03e63a4561a4c71814026867a1f7af6
msgid "GPS (aka Serial3) is for connecting a GPS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:22
#: dc48f83383264500bbb115846b531c9c
msgid "Serial 4/5 contains two serial connections on a single port.  Serial4 is normally used for a :ref:`second GPS <common-gps-blending>`.  Serial5 is a :ref:`debug connection <dev:interfacing-with-pixhawk-using-the-nsh>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:28
#: 7f2eebee464f41e0a6bda9b09fff3e1c
msgid "More details of the exact pins on each port can be found :ref:`here <common-pixhawk-overview>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:31
#: c47f22839abb46d49b7c10dce359a742
msgid "Set-up through the Ground Station"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:33
#: 5f5f970bb61b47dc858b77c9255d2c5e
msgid "The telemetry ports can be configured through the ground station by setting the parameters listed below.  If you are using the *Mission Planner* open the **Config/Tuning \\| Full Parameter List** page."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:35
#: 9b35349a63364b2d82adfbddbd3f9bab
msgid "``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` parameters (where \"x\" is a number from 0 to 4, i.e. :ref:`SERIAL1_PROTOCOL <SERIAL1_PROTOCOL>`) control the protocol or purpose of the serial port.  You will see on wiki pages including the :ref:`Lightware Lidar page <common-lightware-sf10-lidar>` instructions for choosing the appropriate protocol."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:36
#: 2ddefa39e540447e8e33912cdc7775cd
msgid "``SERIALx_BAUD`` (i.e. :ref:`SERIAL1_BAUD <SERIAL1_BAUD>`) sets the baud rate or speed of the serial port."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:37
#: 1f81c5211f254736938a1ea58227659f
msgid ":ref:`BRD_SER1_RTSCTS <BRD_SER1_RTSCTS>` and :ref:`BRD_SER2_RTSCTS <BRD_SER2_RTSCTS>` parameters allow enabling or disabling flow control on Telem1 and Telem2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:43
#: 19254cabafcf415cb5c7521a78e80a22
msgid "MAVLink1, MAVLink2 and Stream Rates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:45
#: 2f2d3ec6487a4259a4d51a099f871364
msgid "For telemetry ports used for MAVLink communication you may select to use MAVLink1 by setting the ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` to \"1\" or MAVLink2 by setting ``SERIALx_PROTOCOL`` to \"2\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:47
#: f256e6ea5ed44439946876dec516619d
msgid "MAVLink2 supports \"signing\" of packets which improves security and flexible length messages so it should be used when possible but some older telemetry radios do not understand MAVLink2 so the default is MAVLink1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:49
#: ea7a6df823d64275a12f3d2a6c56dad9
msgid "MAVLink2 is required to upload and download complex fences from the Ground Control Station."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:51
#: 74963b5ed5c342f7a8c70b0337452aac
msgid "As mentioned on the :ref:`Telemetry Logs page <planner:mission-planner-telemetry-logs>` the rate messages are sent from the vehicle can be controlled using the ``SRx_*`` parameters (i.e. :ref:`MAV2_POSITION <MAV2_POSITION>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:53
#: e18875ae7fe64f3cae71bf75289844bb
msgid "SRx parameters do not directly correlate to the SERIALx port, but rather to the order of the ports which have MAVLink protocol active."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:55
#: fef75dd8c25f4304b83a1f0048f4c7bd
msgid "The Mission Planner's **Config/Tuning |Planner** screen's **Telemetry Rates** drop-downs allow a convenient way to set these parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:60
#: 0b0f475e654e44d5ba84d71ffae493fa
msgid "Due to CPU or bandwidth limitations, the actual rate of the data sent may be lower than the rate requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:62
#: d5bce301ebc44c65ba35f6df48eed684
msgid "Some telemetry systems require specific rates. In order to allow those to be set in the autopilot parameters and not overridden by the GCS, set the rates to \"-1\" for MP, or use the disable option in QGC. However, do not set these before doing the basic autopilot radio calibration in Mission Planner as it forces new values during the calibration and will not restore them after it is finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:66
#: 8d95b7ca4e2a4369aefec49eec7e1faa
msgid "Most ground stations set the desired stream rate by sending the `REQUEST_DATA_STREAM <https://mavlink.io/en/messages/common.html#REQUEST_DATA_STREAM>`__ MAVLink message to the vehicle instead of directly setting the parameters mentioned above.  If done this way, Copter **DOES NOT** save the rate changes to eeprom meaning they will not persist over a reboot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:68
#: 622c071a617648fda790f1de910fa6ec
msgid "In practice users may notice that if the vehicle is rebooted but the telemetry connection is not disconnected and reconnected that the data from the vehicle may be much slower or missing.  I.e. the vehicle's position on the map may not update.  Normally disconnecting/reconnecting with the ground station will resolve this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-telemetry-port-setup.rst:70
#: 8df7b64f675c42e987681843c1e79c70
msgid "See also :ref:`Requesting Data From The Autopilot <dev:mavlink-requesting-data>`"
msgstr ""
